        { term: 'Journal Entry', definition: 'The formal record of a transaction in the accounting system, showing which accounts are debited and credited and for how much.', example: 'To record a $1,000 sale: Dr. Cash $1,000, Cr. Sales Revenue $1,000. The journal entry is the source document for all accounting.' }
