            { label: '$79.99, premium positioning. Estimated demand: 80,000 units/year', consequence: 'CM = $79.99 - $35 = $44.99. BEP = $2,000,000 / $44.99 = 44,454 units. At 80,000 units, profit = (80,000 x $44.99) - $2,000,000 = $1,599,200. Higher profit than the cheap option despite lower volume. Margin of safety = 44%, comfortable. Best balance of risk and reward.', score: 3 },
            { label: '$129.99, ultra-premium like AirPods Pro. Estimated demand: 25,000 units/year', consequence: 'CM = $129.99 - $35 = $94.99. BEP = $2,000,000 / $94.99 = 21,055 units. At 25,000 units, profit = (25,000 x $94.99) - $2,000,000 = $374,750. Despite the huge margin, volume is too low. And margin of safety is only 19%, risky for a new brand competing against Apple.', score: 1 }
