      'Demanding immediate remediation of control weaknesses with SOX disclosure, enforcing audit partner rotation requirements, and independently challenging auditor assessments when red flags appear, scoring 9/9.',
      'The audit committee is the last line of defense between management and shareholders. Its job is not to rubber-stamp the auditors\' work but to independently evaluate audit quality, challenge findings when evidence warrants it, and ensure that internal controls actually function. The failures at Enron, WorldCom, and Wirecard all shared a common thread: audit committees that deferred to management and auditors instead of exercising independent judgment. As Warren Buffett has said: "The audit committee must be the shareholder\'s representative, not management\'s friend."'
