          truth: 'Numbers that look TOO good are actually the biggest red flag. Madoff\'s returns were suspiciously consistent. Enron\'s revenue growth was impossibly smooth. When financial results show no volatility, no bad quarters, and no correlation with industry or economic cycles, they are more likely fabricated than real.',
          explanation: 'Real businesses face real challenges. Revenue fluctuates, margins compress during recessions, bad debts increase when the economy weakens. A company showing steady growth through dot-com busts, recessions, and pandemics is either the greatest business ever created, or a fraud. The odds favor fraud.'
