      ['What is the #1 way fraud is detected?', 'Tips and complaints (43% of cases), according to the ACFE. This is why whistleblower protection laws (SOX 806, Dodd-Frank 922) and anonymous hotlines are critical. External auditors only catch 4% of frauds.'],
      ['What red flags indicate revenue fraud?', 'Revenue growing faster than cash flow, accounts receivable growing faster than revenue, unusual related-party transactions, frequent accounting policy changes, and returns that are "too good to be true" with no volatility.'],
      ['What was Madoff\'s Fraud Triangle?', 'Pressure: investor expectations for consistent returns. Opportunity: no independent oversight, a 3-person auditor (Friehling & Horowitz), self-custody of assets. Rationalization: likely "I\'ll trade my way back to real profits eventually."']
