            { label: 'New customers are a positive sign of business growth, many startups incorporate recently', consequence: 'Three brand-new companies with the same registered agent accounting for 35% of quarterly revenue is textbook revenue round-tripping. This pattern appeared at Luckin Coffee ($310M fabricated), Satyam ($1B fabricated), and Wirecard ($2B fabricated). You need to investigate whether these companies are related parties or shell entities controlled by CloudTech insiders.', score: 0 },
            { label: 'Extremely suspicious, three newly incorporated companies with the same registered agent generating $12M in revenue is a classic shell company / round-tripping pattern. Immediately investigate related-party connections to CloudTech management and trace the cash flows to determine if funds are circular.', consequence: 'Outstanding forensic instinct. Related-party revenue through shell entities is the most common fabrication method. You\'ll want to: (1) Check if any CloudTech officers/directors are connected to these entities, (2) Trace cash flows, did CloudTech fund these companies? (3) Verify the services were actually delivered, (4) Check if payments came from accounts connected to CloudTech. This has all the hallmarks of a Luckin Coffee-style fabrication.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Note the concentration risk in the audit report and move on', consequence: 'This isn\'t a concentration risk issue, it\'s a potential fraud. Simply noting it buries the lede. Three shell companies generating $12M in revenue demand immediate investigation. Failing to investigate could constitute audit negligence if the revenue is fraudulent.', score: 1 }
