      { takeaway: 'Single accounting estimates can swing profits by billions, Amazon\'s $3.9B proves it', detail: 'Useful life, salvage value, and method selection are management estimates with enormous impact. Amazon saved $3.9B/year by extending server lives 2 years. Hertz overstated earnings by $700M through inflated residual values. Every estimate change deserves scrutiny.' },
      { takeaway: 'Depreciation is non-cash, always check cash flow to see through the numbers', detail: 'Depreciation reduces reported income but doesn\'t reduce cash. A company with $50M profit and $30M depreciation generated $80M in operating cash (before other adjustments). EBITDA adds depreciation back to show pre-depreciation earnings, useful but can mask capital-intensity.' }
